            "review_title": "Review at Livannah - Sips & Bites District 2",
            "review_text": "David B\nBruce, Australia1173 contributions\n0\nA cut above other places we have visited\nMay 2026 • Couples\nThis restaurant is quite small but managed to fit in the 18 people in our group. We were told it was French but I am not sure. We had a fixed menu.\n\nWe began with spring rolls and then a pumpkin soup followed it. The soup was perhaps the best I have had in a restaurant. This was followed by fried sea bass in butter sauce. It was excellent. Dessert was chocolate mousse with coffee ice cream.\n\nThe meal was very good. They even provided gluten free options for two in our group.\nRead more\nWritten May 26, 2026\nSakal P\nDear valued customer, \nThank you so much for your visit and for sharing this feedback on Tripadvisor! We're so happy you enjoyed your time with the Livannah team. This is just the beginning, and we’d love for you to keep joining the journey with us for more good sips & fun bites!\n\nBest regards,\nSakal Phoeung\nChef-owner.\nRead more\nWritten May 29, 2026\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
